\section*{Appendix C: UPAS-X Reproducibility Protocol}
\addcontentsline{toc}{section}{Appendix C: Reproducibility Protocol}

\subsection*{C.1 Purpose}
This appendix defines the reproducibility protocol required to ensure that all
UPAS-X simulation campaigns produce bit-for-bit identical results across
independent hardware clusters, execution environments, and temporal runs.

\subsection*{C.2 Deterministic Execution Framework}

\subsubsection*{C.2.1 Cryptographic Seed Locking}
\paragraph{Protocol.}
All stochastic or pseudo-random components of UPAS-X are seeded using a
SHA-256-derived entropy pool synchronized across all MPI ranks.

\paragraph{Seed Definition.}
\[
    S_{\mathrm{global}}
    =
    \mathrm{SHA256}
    \big(
        T_{\mathrm{init}}
        \parallel
        \mathrm{UUID}_{\mathrm{campaign}}
        \parallel
        \mathrm{Config}_{\mathrm{hash}}
    \big).
\]

\paragraph{Requirements.}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Identical seeds across all nodes.
    \item No runtime reseeding permitted.
    \item Seed stored in immutable configuration manifest.
\end{itemize}

\subsubsection*{C.2.2 Deterministic Kernel Execution}
\paragraph{Protocol.}
All CUDA kernels must operate in deterministic mode:
\begin{itemize}
    \item No atomic race conditions.
    \item No non-deterministic warp scheduling.
    \item No floating-point reduction order variability.
\end{itemize}

\paragraph{Constraint.}
\[
    K_{\mathrm{det}}(x,t) = K_{\mathrm{det}}(x,t') \quad
    \forall t,t'.
\]

\subsection*{C.3 Immutable Configuration Manifests}

\subsubsection*{C.3.1 Manifest Structure}
Each UPAS-X run must include a JSON configuration manifest containing:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Ephemeris vectors and reference frames.
    \item PPN gravity flags and relativistic parameters.
    \item BVH construction parameters.
    \item Flux model coefficients.
    \item Random seed and entropy pool hash.
    \item Hardware topology snapshot.
\end{itemize}

\paragraph{Manifest Hash.}
\[
    H_{\mathrm{manifest}}
    =
    \mathrm{SHA256}
    \big(
        \mathrm{Manifest}_{\mathrm{JSON}}
    \big).
\]

\subsection*{C.4 Versioning and Protocol Control}

\subsubsection*{C.4.1 Semantic Versioning}
All UPAS-X campaigns must adhere to strict semantic versioning:
\[
    v = (\mathrm{major}, \mathrm{minor}, \mathrm{patch}).
\]

\paragraph{Rules.}
\begin{itemize}
    \item Major version increments for architectural changes.
    \item Minor version increments for parameter or dataset changes.
    \item Patch increments for bug fixes or documentation updates.
\end{itemize}

\subsubsection*{C.4.2 Protocol Sheet Locking}
Each run must reference a versioned protocol sheet authored by
C.~Matthew~Blackwell. No deviation from the sheet is permitted once execution
begins.

\subsection*{C.5 Cross-Cluster Reproducibility}

\subsubsection*{C.5.1 Hardware Independence}
Reproducibility must hold across:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Different GPU batches.
    \item Different node counts.
    \item Different interconnect topologies.
\end{itemize}

\paragraph{Constraint.}
\[
    R_{\mathrm{clusterA}} = R_{\mathrm{clusterB}}
    \quad \text{(bit-for-bit)}.
\]

\subsubsection*{C.5.2 Temporal Independence}
Runs executed at different times must produce identical results:
\[
    R(t_1) = R(t_2).
\]

\subsection*{C.6 Logging and Audit Requirements}

\subsubsection*{C.6.1 Execution Log}
Each run must produce:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Kernel execution logs.
    \item BVH traversal depth logs.
    \item Flux gradient logs.
    \item Hamiltonian drift logs.
\end{itemize}

\subsubsection*{C.6.2 Provenance Record}
A provenance record must be generated containing:
\begin{itemize}
    \item Manifest hash.
    \item Seed hash.
    \item Protocol version.
    \item Hardware snapshot.
\end{itemize}

\subsection*{C.7 Reproducibility Summary}
The UPAS-X reproducibility protocol ensures deterministic execution, immutable
configuration control, strict versioning, and cross-cluster consistency. These
requirements guarantee that all scientific results derived from UPAS-X are
verifiable, repeatable, and suitable for peer-reviewed publication.